# What must never be built into the image.
#
# The Dockerfile ends in `COPY . .`, so without this file every secret sitting in
# the working directory becomes a layer of a public image — and a layer survives
# deleting the file in a later one. The key is the reason this file exists.
#
# The deployed app does not need `.env`: Render supplies OPENROUTER_API_KEY as an
# environment variable at run time. Nothing below is required for the app to run.

# Secrets. First, and the whole point.
.env
.env.*
*.env
!.env.example
.envrc
.envrc.local
.streamlit/secrets.toml
secrets.toml

# History, which can hold a secret even when the working tree does not.
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes

# Local environments and caches — big, and never the ones the image installs.
.venv
venv/
ENV/
__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.py[codz]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# Editor and tooling state.
.idea/
.vscode/
.claude/
*.log

# Tests do not run in the container, and neither does the headless CLI's scratch
# space. The four working folders are made per session under the system temp
# directory (see Script/workspace.py), so any copy of them here is stale.
Script/test_*.py
Input/
Output/
Previously_Converted/
Manuscripts/
*.book.json

# Documentation and packaging that the running app never reads.
README.md
LICENSE
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
